This phase boundary is useful because the RPC translator is now the only component allowed to reinterpret Core's JSON into our canonical model. The store has already become strict enough to reject malformed or incomplete models; now we make sure the translator never creates them in the first place.

The architecture already specifies the two trickiest address cases: P2PK should use Core's descriptor machinery because Core omits the address from the ordinary script RPC, while P2QPK should simply retain Core's generic Bech32m address and structurally upgrade witness_unknown to P2QPK from the raw v2/32 script.

After 2C.1 passes review, 2C.2 can be much simpler: getblockcount/getblockhash/getblock 2 → DecodeBlock → Store.ApplyBlock, then fork detection/common-ancestor walking and the ≤100-block automatic reorg policy.
